        "title": "The Absolute Value of a Square",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We know that the absolute value operation does nothing to a number if it is non-negative. For example:</p>",
            "readable_text": "We know that the absolute value operation does nothing to a number if it is non-negative. For example:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: |0||= 0;|1||= 1;|2||= 2;|3||= 3; \u22ee]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: |0||= 0;|1||= 1;|2||= 2;|3||= 3; \u22ee]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We can summarize this fact as follows:</p>",
            "readable_text": "We can summarize this fact as follows:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: |x| = x \\quad \\text{ if } \\quad x \\geq 0]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: |x| = x \\quad \\text{ if } \\quad x \\geq 0]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We also know that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x^2]</span> is non-negative for any value of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x]</span>. Therefore, </p>",
            "readable_text": "We also know that [MATH: x^2] is non-negative for any value of [MATH: x]. Therefore,",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\left|x^2\\right| = x^2]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\left|x^2\\right| = x^2]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>where <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x]</span> is <em>any</em> real number.</p>",
            "readable_text": "where [MATH: x] is any real number.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nWe know that the absolute value operation does nothing to a number if it is non-negative. For example:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: |0||= 0;|1||= 1;|2||= 2;|3||= 3; \u22ee]\n\nContent:\nWe can summarize this fact as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: |x| = x \\quad \\text{ if } \\quad x \\geq 0]\n\nContent:\nWe also know that [MATH: x^2] is non-negative for any value of [MATH: x]. Therefore,\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\left|x^2\\right| = x^2]\n\nContent:\nwhere [MATH: x] is any real number."
      },
      {
