        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Simplify the expression <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\left| - \\dfrac{x^2}{10} \\right|.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Simplify the expression [MATH: \\left| - \\dfrac{x^2}{10} \\right|.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Firstly, since <span class=\"math\">[MATH: |{-a}| = |a|,]</span> we can write our expression as</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\left| \\dfrac{x^2}{10} \\right|.]</span></p><p>Then, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication and division:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: |(x^{2})/(10)||=; (|x^{2}|)/(|10|)|=; (|x^{2}|)/(10)]</span></p><p>Since <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x^2 \\geq 0]</span> for any real <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x,]</span> we have that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\left|x^2\\right|=x^2.]</span> Therefore,</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (|x^{2}|)/(10)|= (x^{2})/(10).]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Firstly, since [MATH: |{-a}| = |a|,] we can write our expression as\n\n[MATH: \\left| \\dfrac{x^2}{10} \\right|.]\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication and division:\n[MATH: |(x^{2})/(10)||=; (|x^{2}|)/(|10|)|=; (|x^{2}|)/(10)]\n\nSince [MATH: x^2 \\geq 0] for any real [MATH: x,] we have that [MATH: \\left|x^2\\right|=x^2.] Therefore,\n\n[MATH: (|x^{2}|)/(10)|= (x^{2})/(10).]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nSimplify the expression [MATH: \\left| - \\dfrac{x^2}{10} \\right|.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirstly, since [MATH: |{-a}| = |a|,] we can write our expression as\n\n[MATH: \\left| \\dfrac{x^2}{10} \\right|.]\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication and division:\n[MATH: |(x^{2})/(10)||=; (|x^{2}|)/(|10|)|=; (|x^{2}|)/(10)]\n\nSince [MATH: x^2 \\geq 0] for any real [MATH: x,] we have that [MATH: \\left|x^2\\right|=x^2.] Therefore,\n\n[MATH: (|x^{2}|)/(10)|= (x^{2})/(10).]"
      },
