      {
        "lesson_index": 9,
        "step_index": 5,
        "item_type": "step",
        "step_type": "tutorial",
        "step_id": "5922",
        "content_id": "1831",
        "dom_id": "step-5922",
        "selector": "#step-5922",
        "step_anchor": "step-9",
        "title": "The Absolute Value of a Negative Variable",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We know that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: |x|=x]</span> if <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x \\geq 0.]</span> But what if <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x &lt; 0?]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We know that [MATH: |x|=x] if [MATH: x \\geq 0.] But what if [MATH: x < 0?]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>If a variable is known to be negative, then the absolute value changes it to positive. To turn a negative number into a positive number, we multiply by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: -1.]</span> Therefore, we have</p>",
            "readable_text": "If a variable is known to be negative, then the absolute value changes it to positive. To turn a negative number into a positive number, we multiply by [MATH: -1.] Therefore, we have",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: |x|  = -x \\quad\\textrm{for}\\quad x &lt; 0.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: |x| = -x \\quad\\textrm{for}\\quad x < 0.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To convince ourselves that this is indeed true, let&#x27;s verify it in the case when <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x=-2.]</span> Substituting this value into the above, we get</p>",
            "readable_text": "To convince ourselves that this is indeed true, let's verify it in the case when [MATH: x=-2.] Substituting this value into the above, we get",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: |\u2212 2||= \u2212 (\u2212 2) = 2.\u2713]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: |\u2212 2||= \u2212 (\u2212 2) = 2.\u2713]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nWe know that [MATH: |x|=x] if [MATH: x \\geq 0.] But what if [MATH: x < 0?]\n\nContent:\nIf a variable is known to be negative, then the absolute value changes it to positive. To turn a negative number into a positive number, we multiply by [MATH: -1.] Therefore, we have\n\nContent:\n[MATH: |x| = -x \\quad\\textrm{for}\\quad x < 0.]\n\nContent:\nTo convince ourselves that this is indeed true, let's verify it in the case when [MATH: x=-2.] Substituting this value into the above, we get\n\nContent:\n[MATH: |\u2212 2||= \u2212 (\u2212 2) = 2.\u2713]"
      },
