        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Given that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x\\lt 0,]</span> simplify <span class=\"math\">[MATH: |{-6x}|+2x.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Given that [MATH: x\\lt 0,] simplify [MATH: |{-6x}|+2x.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Firstly, since <span class=\"math\">[MATH: |{-a}| = |a|,]</span> we can write our expression as</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: |6x|+2x.]</span></p><p>Then, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication. This gives</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: |6x|+ 2x|=;|6|\u22c5|x|+ 2x|=; 6 \u22c5|x|+ 2x|=; 6|x|+ 2x|.]</span></p><p>Now, since <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x \\lt 0,]</span> we have that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: |x|=-x.]</span> Therefore,\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 6|x|+ 2x|=; 6(\u2212 x) + 2x|=; \u2212 6x + 2x|=; \u2212 4x|.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Firstly, since [MATH: |{-a}| = |a|,] we can write our expression as\n\n[MATH: |6x|+2x.]\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication. This gives\n\n[MATH: |6x|+ 2x|=;|6|\u22c5|x|+ 2x|=; 6 \u22c5|x|+ 2x|=; 6|x|+ 2x|.]\n\nNow, since [MATH: x \\lt 0,] we have that [MATH: |x|=-x.] Therefore,\n[MATH: 6|x|+ 2x|=; 6(\u2212 x) + 2x|=; \u2212 6x + 2x|=; \u2212 4x|.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nGiven that [MATH: x\\lt 0,] simplify [MATH: |{-6x}|+2x.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirstly, since [MATH: |{-a}| = |a|,] we can write our expression as\n\n[MATH: |6x|+2x.]\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication. This gives\n\n[MATH: |6x|+ 2x|=;|6|\u22c5|x|+ 2x|=; 6 \u22c5|x|+ 2x|=; 6|x|+ 2x|.]\n\nNow, since [MATH: x \\lt 0,] we have that [MATH: |x|=-x.] Therefore,\n[MATH: 6|x|+ 2x|=; 6(\u2212 x) + 2x|=; \u2212 6x + 2x|=; \u2212 4x|.]"
      },
